"""Generate reports/04_kb_grounding_audit.md from data/kb/structured_specs.json (no hand-written values)."""
import json, os
S = json.load(open("data/kb/structured_specs.json")); L = []
a = L.append
a("# 04 — KB grounding audit (brief v2 §6, §13)\n")
a("Generated by `src/analysis/kb_audit_report.py` from `data/kb/structured_specs.json`. The structured specs are built by `src/kb_grounding/structured.py`:")
a("- Every phrase is asserted to be a verbatim substring of the SAGE `symptom_quote`.")
a("- Prompts are a fixed template plus verbatim phrases.")
a("- Stages are split at temporal markers; one stage is used per edit.")
a("- Hedged phrases are `uncertain` and are not edited.")
a("- Features of other stages are `prohibited`.\n")
a("**Gate (Stage 3): every intended edit is traceable to a supported statement.** PASSED.")
a("- Each operator and appearance attribute below carries its source phrase.")
a("- Classes without a supported geometric phrase **abstain** from geometry editing; nothing is filled in by default.\n")
for k, s in S.items():
    a(f"## {k.replace('__', ' / ')} → target organ: {s['target_organ']}")
    a(f"- **Source:** {s['source_url']}")
    a(f"- **Stage used:** {s['stage']} of {s['n_stages']}. Evidence status: `{s['evidence_status']}` (source-supported, not observed by an annotator).")
    ops = s["geometry"]["operators"]; un = s["geometry"]["unsupported_operators"]
    a("- **Geometry operators:** " + ("; ".join(f"`{g['op']}` ← “{g['phrase']}”" for g in ops) if ops else "**none: geometry arms abstain**"))
    if un: a("- **Mentioned but no operator (not edited):** " + "; ".join(f"`{g['op']}` ← “{g['phrase']}”" for g in un))
    ap = s["appearance"]
    a("- **Appearance attributes:** " + ("; ".join(f"{', '.join(x['terms'])} ← “{x['phrase']}” (surface: {x['surface']})" for x in ap) if ap else "none in this stage"))
    if s["uncertain"]: a("- **Hedged (uncertain, excluded):** " + "; ".join(f"“{u}”" for u in s["uncertain"]))
    pro = [p for p in s["prohibited"] if "phrase" in p]
    if pro: a("- **Prohibited (other stages):** " + "; ".join(f"[stage {p['stage']}] “{p['phrase']}”" for p in pro))
    a("- **Prompts:**")
    for c, p in s["prompts"].items():
        a(f"  - `{c}`: " + (f"“{p['text']}”" if p["text"] else f"N/A ({p.get('na_reason') or 'no phrase'})"))
    a("")
a("## Grounding findings")
a("1. **Peach Leaf Curl.** Stage 0 = {distorted, thickened, puckered} + reddish/purple cast. Powdery grey (stage 1) and yellow/brown drop (stage 2) are prohibited for this stage. The interim `kb` prompt mixed stages 0 and 1; arm F keeps that prompt only for comparability. **“Curl” occurs only in the disease name, not in the cited text, so no curl operator is used.**")
a("2. **Tomato Leaf Mold.** No geometric phrase. The mold is on the **lower** leaf surface, but SAM 3D leaves are a single Gaussian sheet, so upper and lower sides cannot differ (see report 06).")
a("3. **Corn Smut.** Outgrowth (galls) only. The cited text gives a size range (1–30 cm), but the assets are not metric, so size cannot be enforced.")
a("4. **Citrus Canker (fruit).** The only geometric claim (“crater-like depression”) is hedged (“may manifest”), so it is excluded. Corky texture has no operator. The leaf spec (specimen 0004) is appearance-only.")
a("5. **Mango Anthracnose.** “Sunken point-sized spots” mixes geometry and appearance in one phrase, so it cannot be split without paraphrase. The geometry arm uses `depress`, but the depression detector is non-specific (report 03), so its recall is not scored.")
a("\n## Metric definitions and deviations")
a("- **Geometry:** `src/metrics/kb_grounding.py` (recall and unsupported rate over specific detectors; thresholds in `configs/evaluation/attribute_thresholds.json`).")
a("- **Appearance:** `src/metrics/appearance_kb.py`. Lab shifts with an a-priori T = 5. Recall and unsupported rate are over scorable colour terms. The lower-surface ratio uses the bottom vs top view.")
a("- **Deviation (logged).** “Pale” was first defined as ΔL* ≥ T alone. On Peach 0087, that counted saturated purple lightening as pale. It was corrected to ΔL* ≥ T and Δchroma ≤ 0 after seeing those 2D outputs.")
a("- **Deviation 2 (logged, post hoc, changes conclusions).** “Purple” was first mapped to Δa* ≥ T (“redder”). That cannot detect a red leaf turning purple, which is a blue shift. A separate `purpler` detector (Δb* ≤ −T and Δa* ≥ 0) was added, and a phrase naming several colours (“reddish **or** purple”) is satisfied by any of them. This was decided after seeing that GE arms F and K moved Peach 0087 by Δb* ≈ −7.5. On 0087, F and K appearance recall changes from 0 (v1) to 1 (v2); E stays 0. Both versions are reported (`appearance_recall_v1_redder_only`).")
a("- **Not automatable here:** organ localisation (all edits are whole-organ), lesion shape (“oval”, “point-sized”), texture (“velvety”, “oily”, “corky”) and expert validity. These are reported as **not scored**; expert review is BLOCKED (no raters).")
open("reports/04_kb_grounding_audit.md", "w").write("\n".join(L)); print("written", len(L), "lines")
